"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KHT9B45F1S0HY3H\",\"title\":\"Green Carbon - Nagpur Industrial Biochar (1 & 2) — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Green Carbon - Nagpur Industrial Biochar (1 & 2)\",\"Green Carbon\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2027\",\"Project code\",\"YHQC\",\"Crediting period\",\"09 May 2026 to 09 May 2036\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"YHQC\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2027\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.2\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"08 Jun 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"07 May 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://green-carbon.co.jp\",\"t\":\"Green Carbon\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.2\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1KBMWD70R1S0VMYW\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KBMWD70R1S0VMYW/prj_1KHT9B45F1S0HY3H/pjd_1KTK4HMVM1S0JKP4/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KBMWD70R1S0VMYW/prj_1KHT9B45F1S0HY3H/pjd_1KR1EHC6Q1S0Y830/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nGreen Carbon - Nagpur Industrial Biochar (1 & 2)\\nGreen Carbon\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2027\\nProject code\\nYHQC\\nCrediting period\\n09 May 2026 to 09 May 2036\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.2\\nSummary\\n\\nAn industrial biochar project by Green Carbon, Inc., comprising two facilities located in Virli and Daryapur, India, each with an annual production capacity of 3,240 MT, utilizing cotton stalk as the primary biomass feedstock.\\n\\nNagpur, India\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 05 Jun 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nExpected 2027\\nIN PROGRESS\\nSite visit\\n\\nIsometric’s qualified VVB conducts a site visit, comparing the project facility against the documentation provided. The required cadence for site visits is defined in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2027\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2027\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n08 Jun 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n07 May 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"